Summary: winemac: per-program ColorDepth for the screen's BITSPIXEL
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c, macdrv_GetDeviceCaps(); written for
 wine-mac-builds.
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: Some old programs (Director projectors among them) refuse to start, or
 draw wrongly, unless the screen is 8 or 16 bits, and a Mac display is
 always 32. AppDefaults\<exe>\Mac Driver\ColorDepth (8, 16, 24 or 32, as a
 string or a DWORD; there is no global value) makes GetDeviceCaps(BITSPIXEL)
 on a display DC in that program return it. win32u already emulates 8- and
 16-bit display modes from what BITSPIXEL says: compatible bitmaps are 8-bit
 DIB sections at 8 bits and 32-bit at 16, and NUMCOLORS and COLORRES follow. PLANES stays 1, and SIZEPALETTE
 and RC_PALETTE stay as in upstream's emulated 8-bit mode (no palette
 device). Other values are ignored with a warning. Without the value
 nothing changes. The display modes Wine reports (EnumDisplaySettings) are
 unchanged.
Uncertain: whether a program needs RC_PALETTE and SIZEPALETTE 256 at 8 bits.
Applies to: wine 11.22, macfixes
Status: 2026-11-18 in a quick build of macfixes 11.22 (VM, not for release;
 smoke and the host OpenGL tests pass). On meeka (macOS 26.7): with the value
 at 8 and 16 a program's screen and memory DCs report that depth, and 32
 without it; color-depth passes there and fails on 11.22-build9. In
 11.22-build10 (CI): the suite passes, this test included (in the build
 VM). With 8 for Webmaster.exe (a Director 7 projector) on meeka, the
 projector's 256-colour check passes but its title draws in wrong colours
 (grey as yellow, red and green): its compatible bitmaps become 8-bit with
 Wine's default colour table. Needs a rework: change only the program's own
 GetDeviceCaps answer and keep win32u's internal bitmaps at 32 bits.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
index 8436284..e3ab15a 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/gdi.c
@@ -211,6 +211,16 @@ static INT macdrv_GetDeviceCaps(PHYSDEV dev, INT cap)
         pthread_mutex_unlock(&device_data_mutex);
         TRACE("cap %d -> %d\n", cap, ret);
         return ret;
+    case BITSPIXEL:
+        /* A ColorDepth set for this program.  win32u already emulates 8- and
+           16-bit display modes (compatible bitmaps, NUMCOLORS, COLORRES)
+           from what BITSPIXEL says. */
+        if (app_color_depth && NtGdiGetDeviceCaps(dev->hdc, TECHNOLOGY) == DT_RASDISPLAY)
+        {
+            TRACE("cap %d -> %d (ColorDepth)\n", cap, app_color_depth);
+            return app_color_depth;
+        }
+        /* fall through */
     default:
         dev = GET_NEXT_PHYSDEV( dev, pGetDeviceCaps );
         return dev->funcs->pGetDeviceCaps( dev, cap );
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h
index 709e688..b8d8ca2 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv.h
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@
 extern bool allow_set_gamma;
 extern bool allow_software_rendering;
 extern bool force_backing_store;
+extern int app_color_depth;
 
 extern UINT64 app_icon_callback;
 extern UINT64 app_quit_request_callback;
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
index 3d68cac..a7311ea 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@ bool retina_enabled = false;
 bool enable_app_nap = false;
 bool accessory_activation_policy = false;
  bool force_backing_store = FALSE;
+int app_color_depth = 0;
 int cocoa_start_timeout = 60;
 
 pthread_key_t macdrv_thread_data_key = 0;
@@ -378,6 +379,20 @@ static void setup_options(void)
         accessory_activation_policy = !wcsicmp(buffer, accessoryW);
     }
 
+    /* The colour depth this program sees for the screen, for old programs
+       that want 8 or 16 bits.  Per program only: there's no global value. */
+    if (!get_config_key(NULL, appkey, "ColorDepth", buffer, sizeof(buffer)))
+    {
+        int depth = 0;
+        /* A string, or a DWORD (whose low word lands in buffer[0]). */
+        if (buffer[0] && buffer[0] < '0') depth = buffer[0];
+        else for (p = buffer; *p >= '0' && *p <= '9'; p++) depth = depth * 10 + *p - '0';
+        if (depth == 8 || depth == 16 || depth == 24 || depth == 32)
+            app_color_depth = depth;
+        else
+            WARN("ignoring ColorDepth %s: not 8, 16, 24 or 32\n", debugstr_w(buffer));
+    }
+
     if (!get_config_key(hkey, appkey, "ForceOpenGLBackingStore", buffer, sizeof(buffer)))
         force_backing_store = IS_OPTION_TRUE(buffer[0]);
 
